  CLAUSE 4 -- THE RUNG: does the protocol teach AT ALL? T0.RET on axis_sep
  +0.1970 +- 0.0791 = 2.5 SE above zero: PASS. (§51 read +0.5295 at 1.8M and +0.0583
  at 150k, so the MAGNITUDE is budget-dependent and is NOT the bar -- a 2 SE
  test asks what the rung means.) On the FORMANT primary §51 measured T0 at
  -0.0059, so T0 is predicted NULL OR NEGATIVE here and reads +0.0099 +- 0.0186;
  a LARGE POSITIVE T0 would contradict §51's ruler calibration.

  CLAUSE 5 -- THE VERDICT. Paired by creature, bar 2 SE, sign unconstrained.
    T1.RET - T1.RET.D         +0.0627  (paired SE 0.0282, 2.2 SE)   <-- PRIMARY
    T1.ORACLE - T1.ORACLE.D   +0.1675  (paired SE 0.0408, 4.1 SE)   <-- CEILING

    (4) THE SOUND-ONLY CAREGIVER TEACHES, AND §51's NULL WAS THE RULER.
    T1.RET - T1.RET.D +0.0627 = 2.2 SE on the quantity a listener hears, with
    the ceiling at +0.1675 = 4.1 SE. T1 reaches 37% of it. The caregiver
    compared two SOUNDS and never looked at the toy; the binding came from
    CO-OCCURRENCE. CHECK THE OTHER BUDGET BEFORE QUOTING THIS -- the dose axis
    is pre-registered precisely because this estimator's SD grows with ticks.

